   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "population": "church",
   "story": "The post had bingo on Thursdays and a fish fry on Fridays. When the radio said shelter in place the commander opened the hall to anyone who needed it, and forty people slept on the bingo tables. The quartermaster kept the cellar: the post's canned stores and the fall raffle prize, a .38 in a walnut presentation box. He said nobody was getting the raffle prize before the draw. Somebody got sick in the hall on the fifth night, and he went down to the cage and locked it from inside.",
